hwlogo (1.0.1) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Keep the hardware state on module unload: set LED_RETAIN_AT_SHUTDOWN so
    the LED core does not switch the logo light off while unregistering
    (affects package upgrade and purge).
  * prerm: unload the module before "dkms remove" - after the .ko is gone,
    modprobe -r can no longer resolve the module name.

 -- Yegor Chuperka <yegor-chuperka@yandex.ru>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 01:33:00 +0200

hwlogo (1.0.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * Initial release.
  * DKMS module exposing /sys/class/leds/huawei::logo for the HUAWEI
    MateBook GT 14 (ENZH-XX) lid logo light.  Talks to the embedded
    controller through the firmware method \_SB.PC00.LPCB.HWEC.ECCD
    (EC registers 0xA4 state / 0xA5 control).
  * hwlogo(1) command line tool, udev rule for group plugdev access and an
    optional systemd unit re-applying the state at boot.
  * Module is signed with the machine's enrolled MOK key by DKMS, so it
    loads with Secure Boot enabled.

 -- Yegor Chuperka <yegor-chuperka@yandex.ru>  Wed, 07 Oct 2026 01:24:44 +0200
